  "facts": [
    "Kingston Bridge, opened in 1828, was built of Portland stone with five elegant elliptical arches, the central span stretching 60 feet and rising 19 feet above the Thames.",
    "In 1870 the bridge celebrated toll removal with fireworks and the dramatic burning of toll gates on Hampton Green, marking it free for all travelers.",
    "Between 1912 and 1914, engineers Mott & Hay widened Kingston Bridge from 25 to 55 feet, adding a new Portland stone façade that mirrored the original classical design."
